// Cortex-M3 with the REAL STM32F100 geometry — the F100 gust failsafe core, as measured on
// silicon rather than as convenient for the image (AFD-088).
//
// This file used to declare 256 KB of flash and 256 KB of SRAM "to cover synth's linear
// memory + initial SP 0x20020000". That is backwards: the platform was sized to fit the
// artifact, so the gate could not reproduce the failure the hardware would have, and an
// image whose stack sat outside physical RAM passed for six weeks.
//
// Measured on an STM32F100 over SWD, 2026-09-05:
//   DBGMCU_IDCODE 0x10016420  -> DEV_ID 0x420, value line
//   flash size reg 0x1FFFF7E0 -> 0x0080 = 128 KB
//   initial MSP of the resident firmware 0x20002000 -> 8 KB SRAM
// Flash is modelled at 0x0 because that is the boot alias the reset vector fetches through,
// which is also where synth places .text.
//
// NO MPU IS DECLARED, AND THAT MATCHES THE SILICON. gale measured MPU_TYPE = 0x00000000
// (DREGION 0) on this part (gale#356) and jess confirmed it independently over SWD, halted:
//     0xE000ED90 MPU_TYPE  00000000     0xE000ED94 MPU_CTRL  00000000
//     0xE000ED00 CPUID     411fc231     (Cortex-M3 r1p1)
// The MPU is OPTIONAL on Cortex-M3 and this part omits it, so any design assuming MPU-based
// isolation, region programming or deny-by-default ON THE IO COPROCESSOR cannot work there —
// not "not yet", but by hardware.
// Do NOT infer otherwise from qemu's lm3s6965evb, which is a Cortex-M3 WITH a PMSA MPU. Same
// core family, different option; that trap cost gale a day.
// passthrough-m3.robot asserts MPU_TYPE reads 0 here, so this platform cannot quietly become
// more capable than the part it stands for.
cpu: CPU.CortexM @ sysbus
    cpuType: "cortex-m3"
    nvic: nvic
    // EXPLICIT 0, and it must stay explicit. Renode DEFAULTS a Cortex-M to EIGHT MPU regions
    // when the platform says nothing: this file omitted the parameter and the emulated core
    // reported MPU_TYPE = 0x00000800 (DREGION 8) while the real STM32F100 reports 0x00000000.
    // Measured, not assumed — the assertion in passthrough-m3.robot failed on its first run and
    // that is how this was found. So "we never declared an MPU" was NOT the same as "there is
    // no MPU here", and a gust:hal isolation design validated on this platform could have
    // assumed eight regions the target does not have.
    numberOfMPURegions: 0
nvic: IRQControllers.NVIC @ sysbus 0xE000E000
    -> cpu@0
flash: Memory.MappedMemory @ sysbus 0x0
    size: 0x20000
sram: Memory.MappedMemory @ sysbus 0x20000000
    size: 0x2000
